			"notes": "## What's Changed\n\nApplied Sorting 2.0.0 adds support for Minecraft 26.1.2 and updates the AE2 terminal integration so the mod no longer takes over space reserved for AE2's own buttons. This should make the sorting controls coexist more cleanly with AE2's UI.\n\n![AE2 Terminal sorted by ID](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f249a663-e3c5-4c8c-85d6-12e046807254)\n\n## Technical Changes\n\nThis release is also a major project-structure rewrite. The codebase has been migrated to a multi-project setup based on [Meatwo310/custom-mdk](https://github.com/Meatwo310/custom-mdk), allowing multiple Minecraft versions and loaders to be maintained from a single branch.\n\nThe v1 codebase is preserved separately at [Meatwo310/applied-sorting-old](https://github.com/Meatwo310/applied-sorting-old)."
		}
